Things to know
==============
The app related actions which are automated under the Android section as below can be done in iOS automation as well.
1. ActivateAppForSwitching
2. CheckAppInstalled
3. DeviceLockAndUnlock
4. InstallApp
5. KeyEvents
6. RemoveApp
7. RunAppInBackground
8. TerminateApp

Note: For iOS, the above actions can be done using the Appium common wrapper methods as well as using the Javascript code.

Mobile Web View
===============
Note: For iOS, Appium can automate WkWebView and UIWebView elements, but not SafariViewController elements.

iOS: Hybrid app and Safari browser: Inspecting WebView elements using the Web Inspector(Simulator)
==================================================================================================
1. Launch Hybrid app and navigate to the WebView page or Launch Safari browser and navigate to the webpage.
2. Open Desktop Safari
3. Enable "Develop" Menu option if not already enabled. Go to Safari > Preferences > Advanced menu and enable "Show Develop menu in menu bar" option.
4. Go to Develop Menu > Select Simulator and then the WebView page / Browser Page > It opens up the web inspector.
5. Copy the CSS / Xpath or any other locator as you would do in Selenium.

For Real Device
===============
Go to Safari > Advanced > Web Inspector and enable it.